      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's hard to shake that feeling, though. You call it \"metabolic struggle,\" but it feels so much more like I've got a little infestation of tiny, shadowy things in there that thrive on making things go wrong. \n\nSince you mentioned they follow \"genetic programming,\" is there any way they can actually coordinate? It doesn't just feel like one random cell acting up; it feels like a whole group of these tiny, unseen entities works together to suddenly pivot the whole starter's character in an instant. Does biology allow for that kind of synchronized, disruptive behavior? It almost feels like they're little agents of chaos working in tandem to throw me off my game.",
      "source": "evaluator"
